# Guiding Hydra's trigger is on the stack at the beginning of combat; in response Bot1 bolts its own Hydra (X = 1, a 2/1).
# The ability still resolves and its controller may say yes (CR 117.3), but the Hydra is a new object in the graveyard
# (CR 400.7) with no counter to remove, so "if you do" (CR 608.2c) is not met and the Ornithopter gets no counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Guiding Hydra
Lightning Bolt
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guiding Hydra.Cast(X: 1)
[T1 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Guiding Hydra)
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Guiding Hydra; Lightning Bolt
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
